From f63dc19423bd47b0ea53feb8cf37569c8ccdd5fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qualcomm-toolbox <169756160+qcom-toolbox@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 18:52:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] umi: FastRPC for the SLPI's sensor PD - it now initializes

The sensor user PD died 36 s after start waiting for its configuration,
which Android serves from user space (sscrpcd; postmarketOS hexagonrpcd)
through reverse FastRPC calls. The kernel now does that job, following
Linux drivers/misc/fastrpc.c for the wire format and hexagonrpcd's
behaviour (linux-msm/hexagonrpc, GPL; no code taken):

- GLINK carries two channels ("IPCRTR" lcid 1, "fastrpcglink-apps-dsp"
  lcid 2) with intents, reassembly and remote intents per channel.
- FastRPC invokes: payload (remote_arg / invoke_buf / phy_page lists,
  fd and crc lists, 128-aligned buffers) in 1 MiB of low RAM at
  0xd3000000 (32-bit DMA, after the Wi-Fi pools), read by the SLPI
  through SMMU streams 0x541-0x543 routed to the non-translating
  display context (sweet_smmu_route_sid), sid 1 in address bits 32+.
- INIT_ATTACH to the sensors PD, remotectl open + register
  adsp_default_listener, adsp_listener init2, then next2 in a loop with
  the nested buffer coding; reverse calls served: remotectl open/close
  and apps_std fopen_with_env, fread, fseek, fclose, fflush, opendir,
  readdir, closedir, stat (read-only), from /private/var/sweet/sensors/
  (the phone's vendor:/etc/sensors, persist:/sensors and sysfs soc0).

On the phone (with a 30 s next2 wait): attach and listener answer 0,
3393 reverse calls are served (soc0, sns_reg_config, the whole
persist registry), then the PD goes quiet and no longer dies. The
listener now waits for the next call without a deadline and the loop
keeps running (not booted yet).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
